<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Data Extension ROWSET for DataExtensionObject[Airlines].

  MANDATORY CUSTOM-COLUMN FIXTURE. Every SFMC Data Extension is CUSTOMER-DEFINED, so none of these
  columns can ever appear in declared build-time metadata. Two are called out deliberately:

    * Loyalty_Tier__c          - a tenant-defined DE column that RUNTIME discovery does list
                                 (see dataextensionfield-airlines.soap.xml), i.e. undeclared at build
                                 time and minted by discovery.
    * Tenant_Promo_Segment__c  - an ILLUSTRATIVE TENANT-DEFINED DE COLUMN that appears ONLY here: it is
                                 in NO declared metadata and in NO discovery result. It exists to prove
                                 the connector passes the FULL source record through to
                                 ExternalRecord.Fields rather than filtering to a known column set, so
                                 the framework's custom-column capture (__mj_integration_CustomOverflow
                                 -> post-sync promotion) has something real to capture. A run in which
                                 this value silently vanishes is a FAILED run.

  Envelope shape is the vendor's own documented DataExtensionObject response
  (par:Results / par:Properties / par:Property{Name,Value}).
-->
<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:par="http://exacttarget.com/wsdl/partnerAPI">
